Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||08-29-2000||11:11 AM||||Okay, someone started this thread in tech ?s but it was pointed out that it should be here, and well, I was thinking about it, and I just felt like sharing my idea of a dream fiero. assuming a budget limit of $250,000. so here goes:<P>Original Car:<BR>I'd say start w/ an '85/86 GT (when they were only available in notch backs still w/ the areo fasade) t-tops, all power options, woofer and all.<P>Supention:<BR>lowering spindles<BR>konis in all the corners<BR>eibrach springs<BR>heavy duty sway bars (front and rear)<P>Brakes:<BR>grand am brake job <BR>slotted rotors <BR>enlarged master cylinder<P>Body:<BR>chop top 3inch<BR>rear window overhang<BR>fieroshop's hood scoops<BR>lighted Pontiac running light<BR>front air damn w/ fog lights and air capture to help push air up to the radiator<BR>The Fi-Air-O dual scoops (resized for the crop top)<BR>and Ideally, a 3 inch or so frame extension, so I could fit my 12" speakers behind the seats and still recline  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>painted high gloss black<P>Engine:<BR>350, 383 stroker (still debating)<P>Tanny:<BR>5 sp Getrag (probrably w/ the 3.63 gears)<P>Wheels:<BR>largest rims possible<BR>I found some rims I really like but I can't find the add right now<BR>low-pro tires<P>Interior:<BR>PISA wrap arround dash<BR>Mr Mike's leather all black<BR>Fiero Store's floor matts<BR>Those stainless steal rocker pannels w/ the fiero emblem<P>Sterio:<BR>Sony CD head (have)<BR>EQ (still looking)<BR>rampage 500 watt amp (have)<BR>appropriate amp for stock woofer replacment<BR>High quality 12s (have cheap ones)<BR>High quality woofer to replace stock<BR>JVC 6x9s (have)<P>Well, that's it. with that for transportation, I don't think I'd ever get out of it.<P>||||reg||10
